From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johan Althoff <teetow@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:14:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(rcontrol): follow the MCP spec for tools

- tools/list put each argument straight into the input schema object;
  arguments go under "properties", and the commands' own input schemas
  were never listed.
- tools/call ignored the arguments and answered before the command had
  run, always with empty content. Arguments are now converted to the
  types the command declares, and the answer is sent when the command's
  promise resolves, with its message and, when the command returns a
  Val, its data as structuredContent. Failures set isError.
- Tool names only had their first '/' replaced and could carry any
  character of an effect's plugin id; they are now MCP-valid
  ([A-Za-z0-9_-], at most 64 characters, long paths shortened with a
  hash), and calls look the command up by name instead of rebuilding a
  path from it, which broke commands containing '_'.
- Only commands available over MCP are listed and callable.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
